The "Guild of Disgruntled Adventurers" level is special.  It allows
teleport and has a diggable floor, which the others don't.  Almost ALL
of the Disgruntled Adventurers are carrying useful wands, potions and
scrolls, and some of them will have "AoLS.  If you allow your insta-
kill pets to clear the level while staying far enough away and out of
sight, NONE of the Disgruntled Adventurers will use their items.  You
can easily end up with over 20 potions of gain level and perhaps 40
potions of full healing after alchemy, plus enough wands of
teleportation, death and digging to never need to look for them again.
Other useful items you will surely find include robes (from monks),
cloaks of magic resistance, and athames from wizards.

> Note that conflict will help too. Purple worms are pets like any other
> so they won't attack monsters of higher level. But with conflict
> they'll attack anything. It's especially satisfying to see your pet
> eat an arch-lich or even the Wizard.

If you want your purple worms to attack high-level monsters without
conflict, take them through graveyards and let them eat all the
wraiths.  Each wraith will always give the worm one level.  Sometimes
this can backfire.  I have had my super-high level purple worms kill
themselves by swallowing the riders on astral.

